{title: Different Gifts}
{subtitle: Romans 12:6–8}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
We are one body in Christ
Each part has a function to [Cm]play
Do not think of yourself [Gm]too high
[Dm]Judge with sober judgment [Gm]today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If it is prophecy prophe[Cm]sy
In proportion to your [Gm]faith
If it is service then serve [Dm]
If it is teaching teach [Gm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If it is encouragement encourage
If it is giving give generous[Cm]ly
If it is leading lead diligen[Gm]tly
[Dm]Showing mercy do it [Gm]cheerfully
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If it is prophecy prophe[Cm]sy
In proportion to your [Gm]faith
If it is service then [Dm]serve
If it is teaching [Gm]teach
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]Let love be genuine always
[Gm]Hate what is evil hold fast to good
[Cm]Devoted in brotherly love
Outdo one another in [Gm]honor
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Cm]Never let your zeal grow slack
Be fervent in spirit serve the [Gm]Lord
{end_of_verse}
